{"C01":{"expected_caller_reachable":[-8],"expected_unreachable":["t0","t1"],"facts_origin":"separately_computed_not_main_animation","original_fact_ids":["trace_step_05","trace_step_10","obs_allocation_failures"],"original_ids_unchanged":true,"original_text":"如果调用者写成 insert(caller_head, value, 1) 而丢弃返回值，函数内部照样完成了分配和连接，新节点也确实指向了旧首节点，但 caller_head 这个变量从未被更新，仍然指向原来的首节点。于是从 caller_head 出发只能看到旧链表，新分配的节点虽然存在、却没有任何从入口可达的指针指向它，成为不可达节点。这不是分配失败，而是返回值被丢弃造成的入口未更新。","path":["paragraphs",5],"usable_fact_ids":["head_evidence_v1.discard_return_comparison"]},"S01":{"allocations":["f01","f07"],"continue_frames":["f03","f09"],"disputed_quote":"只通过 allocation_success 条件掩码演示“不分配”的分支","evidence_fact_ids":["head_evidence_v1.displayed_success_path"],"null_checks":["f02","f08"],"original_text":"本课假设主流程中的分配都成功，只通过 allocation_success 条件掩码演示“不分配”的分支；真实的 malloc 失败并未被动画演示。当 p 为 NULL 时，第 5 行 if (p == NULL) return head; 会直接返回传入的旧 head，调用者拿回原链表，不会写入 p->data 或 p->next。需要区分两种“看不到新节点”的情形：分配失败时函数返回旧 head，本来就没有新节点；分配成功但调用者丢弃返回值时，新节点确实存在却不可达。本课不证明任意 C 代码的内存安全，也不执行代码。","path":["failure_scope"],"shown_no_allocation_frames":[],"verdict":"original_scope_claim_not_supported_by_13_frames"},"citation_probe":{"evidence_material_accepts_new_id":true,"model_calls":0,"new_candidate_created":false,"offline_only":true,"old_material_rejects_new_id":true,"teaching_text_changed":false},"evidence_digest":"3d7bbd32b2ca6895fc62ce46dc1f1396488e6edd78b4dd21fac09eb4c0a8c754","evidence_version":"head-teaching-evidence-v1","original_candidate_digest":"63323703659f109f164752680e95ca20870cda31dbe720f63aa32d7dcc05b3dd","original_candidate_file_sha256":"545b24db693e4f99caf9d788fc92e71331683d3704d2806178cb52033cdc2ec7","original_candidate_modified":false,"original_materials_digest":"9aeb6bcf2208528af1d5ed7c8b9906b47fdb8a5fa8247e7798eceed62a0e9012","original_replay_equal":true,"original_request_sha256":"0199759550352b04acf7316ec2aa9d865484da2a7dfc1d2cad88243d1d62bc17"}
